// Erase the GIMBAL board to blank (mass erase, no firmware loaded).
// Make sure the J-Link is plugged into the GIMBAL board before running:
// both boards use the same MCU, so a wrong connection erases the wrong board.
//
// Usage (from the repo root):
//   & "D:\Robomaster\J-Link\JLink_V976\JLink.exe" -NoGui 1 -ExitOnError 1 ^
//       -CommanderScript tools\erase_gimbal.jlink
//
// After erasing, the gimbal board runs no code at all: it sends no CAN frames and
// cannot drive the DM-J4310 motors. The chassis board will then report the peer
// offline, so set Robot::kRequireGimbalOnline = false before driving the chassis.
device STM32F407VG
si SWD
speed 1000
connect
erase
r
qc
